{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-set-variable","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0044","math_ordinal":56,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH22-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"Vitali's theorem was applied to A_m and the following bound requires A_m to be covered up to a null set; the authority unexpectedly falls back to A in this one sentence.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt222.tex:75","source_normalized_sha256":"a884d2e1d40a0eff777adcfedbafdeb957c04acaf9f0f784de4aebd1de8c1f52","source_text":"$\\mu(A\\setminus\\bigcup\\Cal I_0)=0$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt222.tex:82","target_normalized_sha256":"ad4b0f74ff69f8c3215d2e6818d2bdcafac438dc0b5e686daadf3ede350b3fcd","target_text":"$\\mu(A_m\\setminus\\bigcup\\Cal I_0)=0$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S222"}
{"classification":"mathematical-unmatched-parenthesis","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0045","math_ordinal":231,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH22-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The authority has an unmatched closing parenthesis after F(x); removing it restores the difference-quotient error term used in the next displayed estimate.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt222.tex:290","source_normalized_sha256":"5cbb51616ac93041557bdb94c7d469da0aa3553f519663b68a578062dd10fe07","source_text":"$|F(x+h)-F(x))-hF'(x)|$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt222.tex:303","target_normalized_sha256":"c5feaaa25e6f368c1aca0f1c906eda3915c11eebe45ef3800927f1df2af56ab5","target_text":"$|F(x+h)-F(x)-hF'(x)|$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S222"}
{"classification":"mathematical-duplicated-derivative-symbol","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0046","math_ordinal":503,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH22-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The characterization must equate all four Dini derivatives; the authority repeats the lower right derivative and omits the lower left derivative.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt222.tex:619","source_normalized_sha256":"ed012ab6acf30378fef2b222e7810f1f72bddd983e577109d7663dc31630a4c7","source_text":"$(\\DiniD^+f)(x)=(\\Dinid^+f)(x)=(\\DiniD^-f)(x)=(\\Dinid^+f)(x)=c$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt222.tex:642","target_normalized_sha256":"0b28a1f8f9c65f64331bd1e89d395caf1c52685e4d589382728859d4ef8b4649","target_text":"$(\\DiniD^+f)(x)=(\\Dinid^+f)(x)=(\\DiniD^-f)(x)=(\\Dinid^-f)(x)=c$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S222"}
{"classification":"mathematical-contradictory-derivative-symbol","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0047","math_ordinal":529,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH22-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The same case has already declared DiniD+ finite and equal to Dinid-; its remaining infinite derivative must be DiniD-, as the proof's two dichotomies confirm.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt222.tex:648","source_normalized_sha256":"7688a65cc0440df063d268a4502d2162cb6b69c06e404b971017365824c02502","source_text":"$(\\Dinid^+f)(x)=-\\infty$ and $(\\DiniD^+f)(x)=\\infty$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt222.tex:672","target_normalized_sha256":"3a3c45e8247e00d648521b6c0deba657e863654e2912bda424d86fb3b0655958","target_text":"$(\\Dinid^+f)(x)=-\\infty$ dan $(\\DiniD^-f)(x)=\\infty$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S222"}
{"classification":"mathematical-undefined-variable","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0048","math_ordinal":558,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH22-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"Only g_qn was defined in this construction and the surrounding formulas all use that indexed function; bare g has no definition here.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt222.tex:676","source_normalized_sha256":"cd0aa9856147b6c5b4ff2b7dfee5da20aa38253099ef1b4a64aced233c9afe29","source_text":"$g$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt222.tex:701","target_normalized_sha256":"fffc4f33d6c1ac365837b40c9f3ee4dbc2c13f61bc699b75932511de00ac87c2","target_text":"$g_{qn}$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S222"}
{"classification":"mathematical-undefined-variable","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0049","math_ordinal":567,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH22-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"Only h_qn was defined in the preceding clause and its derivative is used throughout the argument; bare h has no definition here.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt222.tex:684","source_normalized_sha256":"aaa9402664f1a41f40ebbc52c9993eb66aeb366602958fdfaa283b71e64db123","source_text":"$h$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt222.tex:710","target_normalized_sha256":"150331611e871c6a3f124a36dc0574a17c57ded5a884fab0e5574ffb7e10a547","target_text":"$h_{qn}$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S222"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-mesh-factor","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0052","math_ordinal":240,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH22-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The preceding mesh definition and chosen bound use intervals of length 2^{-n}(b-a); omitting (b-a) makes the displayed condition insufficient whenever b-a exceeds 1, while restoring it preserves the proof for all sufficiently large n.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt222.tex:307","source_normalized_sha256":"9496d7508be8836a5f89ba52dd818019eaafbb23c8de79e25cef1a7fc785a146","source_text":"$2^{-n}\\le\\delta$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt222.tex:322","target_normalized_sha256":"2470e4fd72ab79b1e259fbf6845540dabe16c87ebbcdc1cfc611e1df8ce6c0b9","target_text":"$2^{-n}(b-a)\\le\\delta$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S222"}
